    "created_at": "2019-09-23T11:56:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-23T11:58:18Z",
    "body": "`fish_style_pwd_dir_length` along with `truncation_length` works similarly, but not for all the examples you provided.\r\n\r\nThe following will always shorten all parent directories:\r\n```toml\r\n# /home/timvisee/git/project/src/models\r\n\r\n[directory]\r\ntruncation_length = 1\r\nfish_style_pwd_dir_length = 1\r\n# Shows: /h/t/g/p/s/models\r\n\r\n[directory]\r\ntruncation_length = 1\r\nfish_style_pwd_dir_length = 2\r\n# Shows: /ho/ti/gi/pr/sr/models\r\n\r\n[directory]\r\ntruncation_length = 2\r\nfish_style_pwd_dir_length = 1\r\n# Shows: /h/t/g/p/src/models\r\n```\r\n\r\n`fish_style_pwd_dir_length` changes the behavior of the usual truncation; instead of removing the paths when the quantity exceeds the `truncation_length`, it shortens them.\r\n\r\nI'd be open to discussing how we could perhaps expand the directory shortening functionality to be more powerful, or how we can better document existing configuration options. 😄 ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
